+The built-in `local` kind (`src/sources/local.ts`) is the local input Source: it polls nothing and has no channel, and declares `trusted`, so the Policy admits its inputs without sender lists (`SourceScope.trusted`). Inputs reach it through `POST inputs`, whose `Inputs` service (`src/app/input.ts`) stores an `InputEnvelope` and its dedupe receipt, then hands the Trigger to the Engine; it never creates a Ticket. A submission may carry a `channel` (`source`, `thread`, `address`) when the delivering Source can also be written back to — a trusted kind that declares a Channel, such as an edge adapter for a chat platform; `Inputs` copies it onto the Trigger, which is what gives the replies a target, and refuses a channel whose `source` is not the submitting `sourceId`.
 
 That context supplies deployment and commands, setup readiness (`ready`, `configured`, `problem`), configuration, `receive`, `atomic`, and typed `state`. It also exposes Thread reads and metadata writes, Ticket reads and binding/closure commands, Trigger reads, `notify` through Outbox, and `report` for declared health entries.
 
